	<script type="application/ld+json" class="yoast-schema-graph">{"@context":"https:\/\/schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#article","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/"},"author":{"name":"Nagi","@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/#\/schema\/person\/1684e6a75e9f91ae2e33ca2de95b47e2"},"headline":"Chicken Tikka Masala","datePublished":"2018-04-06T10:17:55+00:00","dateModified":"2025-05-09T07:47:47+00:00","wordCount":2026,"commentCount":615,"image":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#primaryimage"},"thumbnailUrl":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/tachyon\/2018\/04\/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0.jpg","articleSection":["Chicken","Chicken Breast","Curries","Gluten Free","Iconic Dishes","Indian Recipes","Main Dishes"],"inLanguage":"en-US","potentialAction":[{"@type":"CommentAction","name":"Comment","target":["https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#respond"]}]},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/","name":"Chicken Tikka Masala - RecipeTin Eats","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/#website"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#primaryimage"},"image":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#primaryimage"},"thumbnailUrl":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/tachyon\/2018\/04\/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0.jpg","datePublished":"2018-04-06T10:17:55+00:00","dateModified":"2025-05-09T07:47:47+00:00","author":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/#\/schema\/person\/1684e6a75e9f91ae2e33ca2de95b47e2"},"description":"Made-from-scratch Chicken Tikka Masala recipe with the signature yoghurt marinated chargrilled chicken smothered in an incredible spice infused curry sauce. It's astonishingly straightforward. To say this is stunning is an understatement!","breadcrumb":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#breadcrumb"},"inLanguage":"en-US","potentialAction":[{"@type":"ReadAction","target":["https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/"]}]},{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#primaryimage","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/tachyon\/2018\/04\/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0.jpg","contentUrl":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/tachyon\/2018\/04\/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0.jpg","width":964,"height":1350,"caption":"Overhead photo of chicken tikka masala on basmati rice in a dark rustic bowl with a piece of naan wedged in on the side."},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#breadcrumb","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Collections","item":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/category\/collections\/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Curries","item":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/category\/collections\/curry-recipes\/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"Chicken Tikka Masala"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/#website","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/","name":"RecipeTin Eats","description":"Fast Prep, Big Flavours","potentialAction":[{"@type":"SearchAction","target":{"@type":"EntryPoint","urlTemplate":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/?s={search_term_string}"},"query-input":{"@type":"PropertyValueSpecification","valueRequired":true,"valueName":"search_term_string"}}],"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/#\/schema\/person\/1684e6a75e9f91ae2e33ca2de95b47e2","name":"Nagi","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/75eae612677fdf550ba9a478ea595902153a0a06b8b27aaf6bc3eddcf6367244?s=96&d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&r=g","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/75eae612677fdf550ba9a478ea595902153a0a06b8b27aaf6bc3eddcf6367244?s=96&d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&r=g","contentUrl":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/75eae612677fdf550ba9a478ea595902153a0a06b8b27aaf6bc3eddcf6367244?s=96&d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&r=g","caption":"Nagi"},"description":"I believe you can make great food with everyday ingredients even if you’re short on time and cost conscious. You just need to cook clever and get creative!","sameAs":["http:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/about-me\/"],"url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/author\/nagi-maehashigmail-com\/"},{"@type":"Recipe","name":"Chicken Tikka Masala","author":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/#\/schema\/person\/1684e6a75e9f91ae2e33ca2de95b47e2"},"description":"Recipe VIDEO above. Make this iconic curry at home!!! It&#x27;s a stunner - and although there&#x27;s an extensive looking list of ingredients, it&#x27;s astonishingly straight forward. Far better than paste in a jar, less oily than restaurants, and you can get everything you need from supermarkets!Spice level: Low. Marinating time: 3 - 24 hours","datePublished":"2018-04-06T21:17:55+00:00","image":["https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/tachyon\/2018\/04\/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0-SQ.jpg","https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/tachyon\/2018\/04\/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0-SQ.jpg?resize=500%2C500","https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/tachyon\/2018\/04\/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0-SQ.jpg?resize=500%2C375","https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/tachyon\/2018\/04\/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0-SQ.jpg?resize=480%2C270"],"recipeYield":["4","4 - 5 people"],"prepTime":"PT15M","cookTime":"PT45M","totalTime":"PT60M","recipeIngredient":["600g\/ 1.2lb   chicken thigh ((boneless, skinless), cut into 3cm \/ 2.2\" cubes (Note 1))","1\/2 cup plain yoghurt, ( full fat best (Greek is fine))","6 cloves garlic (, minced (~1.5 tbsp))","1 tbsp fresh ginger (, grated)","1 tsp garam masala ((Note 2))","1 tsp each salt, cumin, ground coriander, paprika (sweet, normal or smokey)","1 tbsp vegetable oil","1\/8 tsp cayenne pepper ((optional))","Pinch black pepper","2 tsp lemon juice","1 - 2 tbsp oil ((Note 3))","2 tsp turmeric","1 tbsp garam masala ((Note 2))","2 tsp coriander","1 tsp cumin","1\/8 tsp cardamom powder","1\/8 tsp cayenne pepper","3 tbsp (65ml)  vegetable oil ((Note 3))","30g \/ 2 tbsp  unsalted butter OR ghee","1  onion, finely chopped ((brown, white or yellow))","1 tsp salt","2 tbsp fresh ginger (, grated)","6 cloves garlic (, crushed or grated)","1 tbsp paprika ((not smoked))","1 2\/3 cups (400ml)  tomato passata ((tomato puree))","1 2\/3 cups (400ml)  water","100 ml (1\/3 cup + 1 tbsp)  cream ((thickened or pure is fine))","1 tsp sugar","50g \/ 3 tbsp   unsalted butter OR ghee","Basmati rice"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"Chicken Tikka:","itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Combine all ingredients except chicken in a bowl and mix. Add chicken and turn well to coat.","name":"Combine all ingredients except chicken in a bowl and mix. Add chicken and turn well to coat.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-0-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Cover with cling wrap and leave in fridge to marinate overnight (3 hours minimum).","name":"Cover with cling wrap and leave in fridge to marinate overnight (3 hours minimum).","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-0-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Heat 1 tbsp oil in a non stick pan over high heat until smoking. Add half the chicken and spread out. Leave for 2 minutes or until charred. Turn each piece and cook the other side until charred - don't worry if not cooked inside. (Note 4, also Video helpful here) Remove into bowl.","name":"Heat 1 tbsp oil in a non stick pan over high heat until smoking. Add half the chicken and spread out. Leave for 2 minutes or until charred. Turn each piece and cook the other side until charred - don't worry if not cooked inside. (Note 4, also Video helpful here) Remove into bowl.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-0-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Scrape out charred bits left in pan and discard. Add more oil if required and cook remaining chicken.","name":"Scrape out charred bits left in pan and discard. Add more oil if required and cook remaining chicken.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-0-3"}]},{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"Sauce:","itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Wipe skillet with paper towels (or do this part in a pot as you need a lid). Turn heat down to medium high.","name":"Wipe skillet with paper towels (or do this part in a pot as you need a lid). Turn heat down to medium high.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Add oil and butter. When butter is melted, add onions, ginger and salt.","name":"Add oil and butter. When butter is melted, add onions, ginger and salt.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Cook, stirring constantly to ensure it doesn't burn, until the ginger is starting to turn golden and the onions smell sweet, about 5 - 7 minutes.","name":"Cook, stirring constantly to ensure it doesn't burn, until the ginger is starting to turn golden and the onions smell sweet, about 5 - 7 minutes.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Reduce the heat to medium. Add the garlic and paprika, and cook for 2 minutes.","name":"Reduce the heat to medium. Add the garlic and paprika, and cook for 2 minutes.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Add the Curry Sauce Spices, and cook a further 2 minutes, stirring.","name":"Add the Curry Sauce Spices, and cook a further 2 minutes, stirring.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Add tomato passata and water, and mix. Bring to a simmer, then cover and reduce heat to low.","name":"Add tomato passata and water, and mix. Bring to a simmer, then cover and reduce heat to low.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-5"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Simmer for 15 minutes, stirring occasionally.","name":"Simmer for 15 minutes, stirring occasionally.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-6"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Pour curry into a bowl, then use a stick blender to puree until smooth (Note 5).","name":"Pour curry into a bowl, then use a stick blender to puree until smooth (Note 5).","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-7"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Return sauce to skillet. Add cream, sugar and butter. Stir to melt the butter.","name":"Return sauce to skillet. Add cream, sugar and butter. Stir to melt the butter.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-8"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Add chicken, stir. Simmer for a few minutes until the chicken is cooked through.","name":"Add chicken, stir. Simmer for a few minutes until the chicken is cooked through.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-9"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Optional: Sprinkle with a pinch of extra garam masala at the end.","name":"Optional: Sprinkle with a pinch of extra garam masala at the end.","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-10"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Serve over basmati rice, sprinkled with coriander\/cilantro if desired. Try this No Yeast Flatbread as a quick naan!","name":"Serve over basmati rice, sprinkled with coriander\/cilantro if desired. Try this No Yeast Flatbread as a quick naan!","url":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#wprm-recipe-28202-step-1-11"}]}],"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":"4.97","ratingCount":"238","reviewCount":"13"},"review":[{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Thank you Nagi this recipe was delicious! The whole family loved it and thought it was better than take out! Will definitely be making this a regular dish!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Ling"},"datePublished":"2026-09-07"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"This recipe is incredible, I made it for my work colleague, whose favourite meal is Tikka Masala, and he said it was the best he’s ever had.\r\n\r\nI’m a vegetarian myself and would absolutely love to make a vegetable version. I’m just a little stuck on how I could adapt the marinated part of the recipe for vegetables. Any suggestions would be really appreciated.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Tanyia Taylor"},"datePublished":"2026-09-07"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"This was delicious, thank You Nagi. Thé spices were just right and I’m already looking forward to making it again.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Jane"},"datePublished":"2026-08-28"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I feel the same exact way (I love Nagi so much, no complaints at all..She's my favorite!!) This was quite tomatoey. I added some more heavy cream and I'm letting it rest until tomorrow night. Made Nagi's amazing naan bread to go with it, which is always INCREDIBLE!! xo","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cynthia Anne Babcock"},"datePublished":"2026-06-23"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I feel the same exact way (I love Nagi so much, no complaints at all..She's my favorite!!) This was quite tomatoey. I added some more heavy cream and I'm letting it rest until tomorrow night. Made Nagi's amazing naan bread to go with it, which is always INCREDIBLE!! xo","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cynthia Anne Babcock"},"datePublished":"2026-06-23"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Best tikka masala recipe I've found! Didn't have any chicken, so I did prawns and spinach from the freezer. So I just skipped the chicken tikka section, made the sauce and fried prawns in some dry spices when the sauce was done. Added a bit of chicken stock in lieu of chicken. Love all of Nagi's recipes, always so yummy and well written. Plus the portion scaler is sooo handy (I made this tikka masala just for me!).","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Gemma"},"datePublished":"2026-02-27"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Absolutely delicious!!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Diana"},"datePublished":"2026-02-22"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I make this every week it my absolute favourite even my work colleagues love it","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Lynne"},"datePublished":"2026-02-15"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"5 stars...I have made it on rotation.. but I use chicken breast instead.. it's bloody good.. and so tender.. marinate as normal.. quick sear in a hot pan..out while still undercooked, poach in the sauce at the end to cook it through.. divine 🤤 thanks Nagi x","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Nikki"},"datePublished":"2026-01-03"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"5 stars...I have made it on rotation.. but I use chicken breast instead.. it's bloody good.. and so tender.. marinate as normal.. quick sear in a hot pan..out while still undercooked, poach in the sauce at the end to cook it through.. divine 🤤 thanks Nagi x","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Nikki"},"datePublished":"2026-01-03"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Scaled this up for a party of 30. It was absolutely delicious and they loved it.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Amanda Hallam"},"datePublished":"2025-12-29"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"4"},"reviewBody":"I have made lots of Nagi's recipes. They're amazing. The butter chicken was an amazing discovery. \r\n\r\nI though this would be a another level above the butter chicken but I felt the flavour was much less intense. It was more tomatoey and felt a little watered down. The consistency was great and it looked amazing. But the flavour although still nice just didn't feel as intense? Is that just me? Will try again and see if I missed something.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Chick Corea"},"datePublished":"2025-12-15"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Forgot to rate it! 5 stars of course!\r\n(PS: I served this with snow peas and Aldi Roti - which is surprisingly fantastic (find it in the freezer section)","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Eva"},"datePublished":"2025-11-25"}],"recipeCategory":["Mains"],"recipeCuisine":["Indian"],"keywords":"Chicken Tikka Masala, Tikka masala","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","servingSize":"365 g","calories":"582 kcal"},"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#recipe","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/#article"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https:\/\/www.recipetineats.com\/chicken-tikka-masala\/"}]}</script>
