</header><div class="entry-content"><span id="dpsp-post-content-markup" data-image-pin-it="false"></span>
<p class="has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph"><em>A made-from-scratch Chicken Tikka Masala recipe with the signature yoghurt marinated chargrilled chicken smothered in an incredible spice infused curry sauce. It&rsquo;s astonishingly straightforward &ndash; and no hunting down hard to find ingredients!</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Chicken Tikka Masala is an Indian favourite along with <a href="https://www.recipetineats.com/butter-chicken/">Butter Chicken</a> and <a href="https://www.recipetineats.com/biryani/">Biryani</a>. Serve with <a href="https://www.recipetineats.com/how-to-cook-basmati-rice/">Basmati Rice</a>, else add a side of chewy and fluffy <a href="https://www.recipetineats.com/naan-recipe/">Naan</a> or basic <a href="https://www.recipetineats.com/easy-soft-flatbread-yeast/">Homemade Flatbreads</a> to mop up the sauce!</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image"><img fetchpriority="high" loading="eager" decoding="async" width="964" height="1350" src="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0.jpg" alt="Overhead photo of chicken tikka masala on basmati rice in a dark rustic bowl with a piece of naan wedged in on the side." class="wp-image-28187" srcset="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=1 964w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=0.8 771w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=0.67 646w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) calc((100vw - 40px) * .31623931623931625), calc(100vw - 200px)" data-pin-media="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_0.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center" id="h-chicken-tikka-masala"><strong>Chicken Tikka Masala</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There are various tales about the <strong>origins of Chicken Tikka Masala</strong>, and most are along the lines of the following: That a British aristocrat was served Chicken Tikka (chicken on skewers chargrilled in a tandoor) and sent it back to the kitchen, complaining it was dry. In response to which the enterprising chef added a curry sauce and sent it back out again where it was well received.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And thus, <strong>one of the most popular curries in the world was born</strong>. 🙂 And even though it&rsquo;s not a traditional Indian dish, the roots of it certainly are!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Proper Chicken Tikka Masala served at good Indian restaurants is made with yoghurt marinated chicken which is then chargrilled so it has that gorgeous smokey flavour.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Regretfully, I don&rsquo;t have a tandoor sitting in the middle of my kitchen. So this recipe aims to replicate the flavour using my good old stove.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="857" src="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_1-landscape.jpg" alt="Close up of Chicken Tikka Masala over rice in a dark bowl, garnished with coriander / cilantro." class="wp-image-28218" srcset="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_1-landscape.jpg?resize=1200%2C857&amp;zoom=1 1200w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_1-landscape.jpg?resize=1200%2C857&amp;zoom=0.86 1032w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_1-landscape.jpg?resize=1200%2C857&amp;zoom=0.64 768w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_1-landscape.jpg?resize=1200%2C857&amp;zoom=0.54 648w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) calc((100vw - 40px) * .31623931623931625), calc(100vw - 200px)" data-pin-media="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_1-landscape.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center" id="h-how-to-make-chicken-tikka-masala"><strong>How to make Chicken Tikka Masala</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We start off with a Chicken Tikka yoghurt marinade for chicken thighs. Thighs, my friends. Not breast! We need juicy meat for this recipe because we&rsquo;re going to blast it with some serious heat to replicate the char grilled flavour of Chicken Tikka!</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="857" src="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Marinade-for-Chicken-Tikka.jpg" alt="Marinade for chicken tikka made with yoghurt, spices, lemon juice, salt and oil." class="wp-image-28189" srcset="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Marinade-for-Chicken-Tikka.jpg?resize=1200%2C857&amp;zoom=1 1200w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Marinade-for-Chicken-Tikka.jpg?resize=1200%2C857&amp;zoom=0.86 1032w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Marinade-for-Chicken-Tikka.jpg?resize=1200%2C857&amp;zoom=0.64 768w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Marinade-for-Chicken-Tikka.jpg?resize=1200%2C857&amp;zoom=0.54 648w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) calc((100vw - 40px) * .31623931623931625), calc(100vw - 200px)" data-pin-media="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Marinade-for-Chicken-Tikka.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Leave it to marinade for at least 3 hours, preferably overnight. Then heat your pan until it&rsquo;s smoking hot &ndash; and I mean&nbsp;<i>smokin&rsquo; hot!!</i> &ndash; then cook those chicken pieces so the yoghurt coating gets chargrilled.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="964" height="1350" src="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_7.jpg" alt="Close up of Chicken Tikka cooking in a black skillet, charred." class="wp-image-28184" srcset="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_7.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=1 964w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_7.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=0.8 771w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_7.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=0.67 646w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) calc((100vw - 40px) * .31623931623931625), calc(100vw - 200px)" data-pin-media="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_7.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After that, we make the sauce, then toss the chicken back in to bring all the flavours together. And this is the vision that you will be bestowed with &ndash; your very own homemade Chicken Tikka Masala, made from scratch. With the signature deep orangey red sauce, wafting with aromatic curry flavour, smothering chicken with a beautiful chargrilled flavour.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center" id="h-tikka-masala-is-deceptively-easy"><strong>Tikka Masala is deceptively easy!</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This isn&rsquo;t your everyday mid week meal. The ingredients list in the recipe looks alarmingly long, but it&rsquo;s deceptive because there are duplicate ingredients. And we&rsquo;re making a serious curry here! We can&rsquo;t skimp on flavour!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And though the list might be long, here&rsquo;s the best news &ndash;&nbsp;<strong>no hunting down unusual&nbsp;</strong><b>ingredients. </b>You&nbsp;can get every single ingredient from the major supermarkets here in Australia (Woolies, Coles, Harris Farms, most Aldi&rsquo;s and large IGA&rsquo;s).</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="964" height="1350" src="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_9.jpg" alt="Chicken Tikka Masala in a black skillet garnished with coriander / cilantro." class="wp-image-28186" srcset="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_9.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=1 964w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_9.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=0.8 771w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_9.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=0.67 646w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) calc((100vw - 40px) * .31623931623931625), calc(100vw - 200px)" data-pin-media="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_9.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-recipe-references"><strong>RECIPE REFERENCES</strong></h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This recipe is the result of a mountain of reading, researching, tasting and cooking we did in pursuit of the ultimate Tikka Masala recipe for the home cook.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We visited some of our favourite Indian restaurants in Sydney just to taste the chicken tikka masala, and recounted our memories of curries we experienced in the UK and India.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We looked at existing recipes by authors both well known (Madhur Jaffrey and Heston Blumenthal) and unknown, including many Indian food bloggers. We even watched Youtube videos in Hindi and went to the library and dug up faded old Indian cookbooks!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We pulled out the best bits from every source of inspiration as well as adding our own ideas to come up with this recipe!</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center" id="h-difference-between-chicken-tikka-masala-and-butter-chicken"><strong>Difference between Chicken Tikka Masala and Butter Chicken</strong></h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In case you are wondering about the difference between&nbsp;Chicken Tikka Masala and&nbsp;<a href="https://www.recipetineats.com/butter-chicken/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Butter Chicken</a>, the main thing is the char grilled flavour of the chicken which Butter Chicken does not have. Also, the sauce of Tikka Masala is more intense and complex. 🙂</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="964" height="1350" src="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_4-1.jpg" alt="Photo of chicken tikka masala on basmati rice in a dark rustic bowl with a piece of naan wedged in on the side. Pickled red cabbage and skillet of Chicken Tikka Masala in the background." class="wp-image-28182" srcset="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_4-1.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=1 964w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_4-1.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=0.8 771w, https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_4-1.jpg?resize=964%2C1350&amp;zoom=0.67 646w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) calc((100vw - 40px) * .31623931623931625), calc(100vw - 200px)" data-pin-media="https://www.recipetineats.com/tachyon/2018/04/Chicken-Tikka-Masala_4-1.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For curry lovers everywhere, <strong>it&rsquo;s truly worth making your own curry from scratch at least once in your life</strong>. Like <a href="https://www.recipetineats.com/thai-red-curry-with-chicken/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Thai Red Curry</a>, a store bought curry paste (even a really great one) simply doesn&rsquo;t compare. If I were to make this using a jar of paste, I would pimp it up quite a bit with fresh garlic, ginger and spices, and it would be not much less effort than making it from scratch!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I really hope you love this. This is a recipe that my brother and I developed together, tag teaming with the recipe until we &ldquo;got it right&rdquo; (meaning, as close as possible to good Indian restaurants).&nbsp;Hope you enjoy! <em><strong>&ndash; Nagi x</strong></em></p>



<div style="border: 2px solid #b8b8b8; padding: 2px 20px 2px 20px;">
