	<ul class="children">

	<li class="comment even depth-2" id="comment-2162749">
	<article id="article-comment-2162749">

		
		<header class="comment-header">
			<p class="comment-author">
				<img alt='' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d87e9b0564279c63dd6f7b42e3b922f9023118c0784d06e893974b96a097b82?s=40&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&#038;r=g' srcset='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d87e9b0564279c63dd6f7b42e3b922f9023118c0784d06e893974b96a097b82?s=80&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&#038;r=g 2x' class='avatar avatar-40 photo' height='40' width='40' loading='lazy' decoding='async'/><span class="comment-author-name">Chris W</span> <span class="says">says</span>			</p>

			<p class="comment-meta"><time class="comment-time">September 25, 2026 at 4:22 pm</time></p>		</header>

		<div class="comment-content">
			
			<p>This is exactly what I do &#8211; chargrill the chicken on a ripping hot Weber to get that smokey, tandoor flavour.  Just make sure you oil the bars well as the marinade is very sticky.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="comment-reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-2162749" data-commentid="2162749" data-postid="28180" data-belowelement="article-comment-2162749" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Chris W" aria-label="Reply to Chris W">Reply</a></div>
		
	</article>
	</li><!-- #comment-## -->
</ul><!-- .children -->
</li><!-- #comment-## -->

	<li class="comment odd alt thread-even depth-1" id="comment-2003154">
	<article id="article-comment-2003154">

		
		<header class="comment-header">
			<p class="comment-author">
				<img alt='' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7cc08274b995df9af4ad3e146ab75dc30ba4f051d6b904e19600c9e6178cfc4c?s=40&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&#038;r=g' srcset='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7cc08274b995df9af4ad3e146ab75dc30ba4f051d6b904e19600c9e6178cfc4c?s=80&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&#038;r=g 2x' class='avatar avatar-40 photo' height='40' width='40' loading='lazy' decoding='async'/><span class="comment-author-name">Amber</span> <span class="says">says</span>			</p>

			<p class="comment-meta"><time class="comment-time">April 4, 2026 at 5:00 am</time></p>		</header>

		<div class="comment-content">
			
			<p>I love nagis butter chicken recipe so this one felt like a bit of faff while I was making it. Extra steps, loads of spices used, blending requirement etc. But wow. It’s much closer to a ‘real’ curry than the butter chicken and the family absolutely loved it. Used chicken breast an as others have said just don’t overcook it at the beginning and it’s fine. I’ll have to perfect my charring technique but otherwise, wow &#8211; what a curry. Yum! Thanks nagi.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="comment-reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-2003154" data-commentid="2003154" data-postid="28180" data-belowelement="article-comment-2003154" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Amber" aria-label="Reply to Amber">Reply</a></div>
		
	</article>
	</li><!-- #comment-## -->

	<li class="comment even thread-odd thread-alt depth-1" id="comment-1992555">
	<article id="article-comment-1992555">

		
		<header class="comment-header">
			<p class="comment-author">
				<img alt='' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4c432e2866ae5e720436cb7e5e2053bef3de5602ae71d6539dd1ddb54d2f6a32?s=40&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&#038;r=g' srcset='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/4c432e2866ae5e720436cb7e5e2053bef3de5602ae71d6539dd1ddb54d2f6a32?s=80&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&#038;r=g 2x' class='avatar avatar-40 photo' height='40' width='40' loading='lazy' decoding='async'/><span class="comment-author-name">Kim</span> <span class="says">says</span>			</p>

			<p class="comment-meta"><time class="comment-time">March 19, 2026 at 9:01 pm</time></p>		</header>

		<div class="comment-content">
			
			<p>I figured since we are both in Australia that a tablespoon was 20ml&#8230;?</p>
		</div>

		<div class="comment-reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-1992555" data-commentid="1992555" data-postid="28180" data-belowelement="article-comment-1992555" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Kim" aria-label="Reply to Kim">Reply</a></div>
		
	</article>
	<ul class="children">

	<li class="comment odd alt depth-2" id="comment-2000492">
	<article id="article-comment-2000492">

		
		<header class="comment-header">
			<p class="comment-author">
				<img alt='' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5e292beb4004ca234f1c9eab430f4561d974384824bf95fbe5847f756e1f06c9?s=40&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&#038;r=g' srcset='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5e292beb4004ca234f1c9eab430f4561d974384824bf95fbe5847f756e1f06c9?s=80&#038;d=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.recipetineats.com%2Ftachyon%2F2024%2F06%2Favatar-guest-temp-cache-bust-duplicate.png&#038;r=g 2x' class='avatar avatar-40 photo' height='40' width='40' loading='lazy' decoding='async'/><span class="comment-author-name">Ann</span> <span class="says">says</span>			</p>

			<p class="comment-meta"><time class="comment-time">March 31, 2026 at 8:01 am</time></p>		</header>

		<div class="comment-content">
			
			<p>No, use 15ml tablespoons for all Nagi’s recipes as she does. It may not matter for smaller amounts like 1 Tbsp, but for 6 Tbsp it definitely could matter!</p>
		</div>

		<div class="comment-reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-2000492" data-commentid="2000492" data-postid="28180" data-belowelement="article-comment-2000492" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Ann" aria-label="Reply to Ann">Reply</a></div>
		
	</article>
	</li><!-- #comment-## -->
</ul><!-- .children -->
</li><!-- #comment-## -->

